  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Testing Laboratories contracting under NAICS 541380 has recorded $373M in federal contract obligations year to date in FY2026. The market has 2,806 awards so far, and the average award size is $133K. Obligations fell 35.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations peaked at $671M in FY24 and then moved to $574M in FY25 before the current FY26 to date total of $373M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $171M in obligations, followed by civilian health and veterans agencies. A mix of defense, health, agriculture, and transportation agencies drive demand. The largest individual vendors include AGILE DEFENSE, LLC at $31.4M and MERRICK & COMPANY at $28.8M, with several other contractors receiving between $10.7M and $21.7M. This profile reflects a concentrated buyer base and multiple mid-sized suppliers across federal technical, health, and research missions. For contractors evaluating opportunities, award counts and average award size show an active market with many smaller awards alongside a few larger, program-level obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
